## FENCES, PARTITION, HOLDS
- **Git:** root history writes only `worktree add -b`, ONE commit, ONE `merge --no-ff`. No `worktree remove`, `fetch`, `push`, `stash`, `reset`, `rebase`, `amend`, `prune`, `gc`, `clean`. In the code repo: `gh api -X GET` only; you clone nothing and edit no file there.
- **HTTP:** `gh api -X GET` to the code repo; the Jira site named in the project's `.env` for GETs and the one comment POST (python `-I`, token in-process, never printed). No mailbox, no demo, no hosted or production host, no package or container registry. No az, ssh, docker, npm, tests, build, deploy, mail, chat, Artifact, Docs, PR, merge of any PR, card or `decision_queue.sh`; no message to any human; no comment or edit on any PR.
- **Partition, from this side:** yours are root `main` for the one merge; `.tools/wt-b1576-rec`, `records/b1576`; your Step-0 copy, STATUS, `Briefs/2026-11-15_B1576_evidence/`, `.tools/b1576/`; the one comment on PCOMP-128. **Read-only:** the gate folder in Tuesday's `briefs/`, the B1569 STATUS and evidence, `.tools/b1486/scripts/` and `.tools/b1552/scripts/` (copy, never edit). **Not yours:** every Jira key but the one comment (PCOMP-128 is never moved or edited), `2_Project_Files` code, `.tools/b1569` and every other seat's tree, open PR #85. **From the other side:** no live seat's kit (MPS-M138, MPS-M139, HPSM-POC-H165, NexusAI-N130) names the Composer folder or Jira PCOMP; the sibling records seats of this wave (R233 MPS, R234 HPSM-POC) write other projects' trees and other Jira keys only.
- **Standing lines:** PRIOR-WORK CHECK (above); no message to any human; Jira writes: the one comment, only under COMMENT-128 POST; never delete (quarantine); never print a credential; no word added to any user-facing text; `always-verify-and-check` and `no-skip-on-failure`: a red you cannot explain is a STOP.
- **HOLDS:** no deploy and no statement about the hosted state beyond "NOT DEPLOYED" as a repository fact; no ruling of your own; no move, label edit or new Task on any issue; no edit of `DEPLOY.md`; no new wording lane (the Minor and items (2) and (5) are row #485 and PCOMP-128).

